{"format":1,"kind":"pfa","id":"pfa-1960","version":"pfa-1960-24601141","year":1960,"season":"1960","label":"NFL (computed)","local":false,"source":{"provider":"Pro Football Archives","edition":"The 1960 NFL season, computed","compiler":"Pro Football Archives (the facts: starts, positions, box scores); the overall ours, computed from them and read off Madden NFL 2002 (maddenratings.net)","url":"https://www.profootballarchives.com/1960nfl.html","retrieved":"2026-11-09","method":"computed","rawScale":"value","conversion":"Ours, computed: no game rated this NFL season. Each player's season value (his club's credit, its points per game against the league's to the power 0.25, offence and defence apart, shared out: the offensive line by starts; quarterbacks, backs, receivers and tight ends by production, rushing and receiving yards, 0.2 a passing yard, 40 a touchdown and less 60 an interception thrown, and by starts; defenders two thirds by starts and one third by plays, 2 a sack where recorded, 1.5 an interception, 1 a fumble recovered, 1 a return touchdown; kickers by field goals, extra points and accuracy against the league) is ranked among the league-season's players at his game position (ties by starts, then games played) and read off Madden NFL 2002's overalls at that position (the 2001 season: maddenratings.net's 31 team spreadsheets, punters left out), as many of each Madden team's best as the season carries per club, by linear interpolation; rounded and held to 1–99. Then each club moves toward its results: its target is T = μ + √r × S ÷ m, where S is its Simple Rating System (its margins by least squares with a home edge, the NFL's ratings summing to nought) from the season's 78 games, r = 0.603 their reliability, m = 1.944 points of margin a game for each point of the strength the match model plays (its lineup's offence and defence, their mean), measured over 160,000 simulated games under the season's rules, and μ = 78.36 the clubs' mean strength before the move. Every player of a club moves by one whole number and its best few by one more, held to 1–99 and never past a teammate rated above him, whichever brings the club nearest its target: −4 to +4 points this season. The results count twice, by design: the credit's points for and against place a club's players at their positions and weigh its offence against its defence, and the move then sets the club's level from its margins, wherever the credit left it. Facts from Pro Football Archives; the weights tuned once on 2001–2005 against the next season's Madden launch ratings, then frozen."},"map":"nfl1960","clubs":[{"id":"nfl-cleveland-browns","name":"Cleveland Browns","code":"CLE","league":"NFL","country":"840","col":"oklch(0.72 0.16 242)","str":82.3,"squad":[["Milt Plum","QB",96],["Len Dawson","QB",56],["Jim Brown","RB",90],["Bobby Mitchell","RB",85],["Prentice Gautt","RB",60],["Rich Kreitling","WR",75],["Ray Renfro","WR",74],["Leon Clarke","WR",70],["Fred Murphy","WR",63],["Gern Nagler","TE",76],["A.D. Williams","TE",53],["Dick Schafrath","OL",94],["Gene Hickerson","OL",93],["Jim Ray Smith","OL",93],["John Morrow","OL",93],["Mike McCormack","OL",93],["Gene Selawski","OL",54],["John Wooten","OL",54],["Bob Gain","DL",93],["Paul Wiggin","DL",80],["Floyd Peters","DL",73],["Jim Houston","DL",65],["Jim Marshall","DL",64],["Larry Stephens","DL",63],["Galen Fiss","LB",83],["Vince Costello","LB",71],["Walt Michaels","LB",69],["Jim Shofner","CB",88],["Bernie Parrish","CB",80],["Bobby Franklin","S",87],["Don Fleming","S",77],["Rich Mostardi","S",57],["Sam Baker","K",88]]},{"id":"nfl-green-bay-packers","name":"Green Bay Packers","code":"GBP","league":"NFL","country":"840","col":"oklch(0.72 0.16 198)","str":82.3,"squad":[["Bart Starr","QB",73],["Lamar McHan","QB",70],["Jim Taylor","RB",95],["Paul Hornung","RB",94],["Tom Moore","RB",67],["Max McGee","WR",86],["Boyd Dowler","WR",80],["Lew Carpenter","WR",67],["Paul Winslow","WR",56],["Gary Knafelc","TE",72],["Ron Kramer","TE",69],["Bob